1
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
What kind of guys gamble with the boss's money, swipe a killer's
Cadillac, and party on the mob's credit card?

2
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Wise Guys is a comedy, crime film directed by Brian De Palma.

3
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Harry Valentini and Moe Dickstein are both errand boys for the Mob.

4
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:30,000
When they lose $250,000, they are set up to kill each other.

5
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
But they run off to Atlantic City and comedy follows.

6
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Harry Valentini, played by Danny DeVito.

7
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:18,000
Moe Dickstein, played by Joe Piscopo.

8
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Bobby DiLea, played by Harvey Keitel.

9
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Marco, played by Ray Sharkey.

10
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Anthony Castelo, played by Dan Hedaya.

11
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:42,000
Frank "The Fixer" Acavano, played by Louis Albano.

12
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
Wise Guys is a 1986 American black comedy crime film directed by Brian De Palma and produced
by Aaron Russo from a screenplay written by George Gallo and Norman Steinberg.

13
00:59:48,000 --> 00:59:54,000
It stars Danny DeVito and Joe Piscopo as two small-time mobsters from Newark, New Jersey, and
features Harvey Keitel, Ray Sharkey, Lou Albano, Dan Hedaya, and Frank Vincent.

14
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:30,000
De Palma later called it "a movie I wish I hadn't done...

15
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
The studio changed their minds and didn't want to make it.

16
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
They just wanted us to go away.

17
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:18,000
I should have just taken my money and walked instead of dealing
with a studio that didn't want to make the movie."

18
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:54,000
The film explores themes of gangster, mafia, horse racing.

19
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:30,000
The tone is lighthearted.
